// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The pinned truth for the Python traceback explainer.
//
// Every traceback below was printed by a real interpreter on 2026-10-27:
// CPython 3.13.16, 3.12.3 and 3.11.17 in the build container (default
// exception hook, scripts at /home/ana/netops in a private mount namespace,
// PYTHON_COLORS=0 unless the vector says otherwise), and CPython 3.14.2 (the
// site's Pyodide 314.0.7 build, run in Node, through the traceback module).
// No 3.15 interpreter was available, so no vector is 3.15 output. A few
// inputs are real output transformed (CR LF, no-break spaces, an indented
// copy, a cut copy) and each says so; the refusals are not tracebacks.
//
// The expected structure was NOT produced by this engine: a harness
// (oracle.py) ran each script again and wrote, from the exception objects,
// the types, messages, notes, links, frames, positions, whether CPython
// printed markers for each frame (its own format_frame_summary) and the kind
// of expression under them (an ast parse of the marked segment). The file
// kinds follow the documented path rule, written a second time in the
// generator. The readings (where to look first, the release range, the
// notes, the sensitive findings, the redacted copies) were written by hand
// from the rules in the tool's documentation. Generated by
// write_vectors_ts.py from make_vectors.py's data; do not edit by hand.
// ============================================================================

